      en: 'In Dibar village, Patnitala upazila, a single octagonal granite pillar rises from the middle of a large tank. Tradition holds that the pond was dug by Divya (Divyoka), leader of the 11th-century Kaibarta revolt against the Pala kings, and that the pillar commemorates the victory; some attribute it to his successor Bhima.\n\nHow much of the pillar shows depends on the water level, and a good part of it is believed to stand below the surface. Its upper section has bands of mouldings. How such a large monolith was brought here and raised in the middle of a pond remains a source of wonder.\n\nTrees line the high banks and the village around is peaceful. Sitting on the bank on a winter afternoon, looking at the pillar, it is easy to think back to one of the earliest recorded peasant and fisherfolk uprisings in Bengal.'
