      en: 'This single-domed mosque stands beside the Khaniadighi tank, wrapped in mango orchards in Shibganj, Chapainawabganj. It is believed to date from the Sultanate period, probably the late 15th or early 16th century, and is also known locally as the Rajbibi Mosque.\n\nA large dome over a square prayer hall, with a verandah in front, follows a familiar Sultanate pattern. Fine terracotta covers the walls inside and out; the creepers and hanging motifs around the mihrabs are especially beautiful. The mosque takes its name from the old tank beside it.\n\nShaded by mango trees, with still water and birdsong all around, it is a deeply peaceful spot. Come in March when the mango blossom scents the air, or on a winter morning in soft light.'
