      en: 'Sri Sri Anukulchandra Thakur was born in 1888 in Himaitpur village near Pabna town, and went on to found the Satsang spiritual and social movement. He established his first ashram here and began work in education, medicine and social service. Before Partition he moved to Deoghar in India, but as his birthplace Himaitpur remains deeply sacred to his followers.\n\nThe large ashram compound holds temples, prayer halls, memorial buildings and well-kept gardens. It is clean and peaceful, and devotees visit throughout the year.\n\nDuring the month of Bhadra (August–September) the Thakur’s birth anniversary draws many thousands of devotees from Bangladesh, India and beyond, and the whole area fills with kirtan, prayer and the sharing of prasad.'
