      en: 'Near the Karatoya in Shahzadpur, Sirajganj, stand the shrine of the Sufi saint Hazrat Makhdum Shah Daula Shahid and an old mosque beside it. Local tradition says he came from Arabia with companions to preach Islam, and fell in battle against a local ruler; the name Shahzadpur is also popularly linked to him.\n\nThe neighbouring mosque has many domes and is often attributed to the Sultanate or early Mughal period, though its exact date is debated. Several more graves in the compound are believed to be those of his companions.\n\nDevotees visit throughout the year, and numbers swell during the annual urs. The Rabindra Kachharibari is close by, so one trip covers two very different sides of Shahzadpur’s heritage.'
